# The build reads Go sources, go.mod/go.sum and the embedded web assets. Nothing
# else belongs in the context.
#
# .git matters most: it changes on every commit, so leaving it in would bust the
# `COPY . .` layer cache even when no source file changed.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local build output. dist/ alone is ~29 MB of cross-compiled binaries.
bin/
dist/

# Not compiled into anything.
docs/
scripts/
deploy/
*.md
!README.md

# Sample configuration and the developer's own nav.yaml, which lives at the
# repository root and therefore changes on every local edit. The binary reads
# config through --file/--source at runtime, never from the image, so shipping
# these would cost a layer rebuild per content change for nothing.
nav.yaml
nav.*.yaml
custom.css.example

# Runtime state, never image content.
ghome-cache.yaml
*.tmp

.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
